WEBVTT

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.490
<i>Christmas 2013.</i>

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.660
<i>On a small outdoor 
stage in Kotodai Park,</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.410
<i>we performed our debut concert.</i>

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.670
<b>SENDAI Student Metal Band Concert</b>

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.420
<i>The audience was small, 
and we had only one song,</i>

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.920
Nanase Yoshino 
Hisami Nanami 
Okamoto Miyu 
Katayama Minami 
Hayashida Airi 
Kikuma Kaya 
Shimada Mayu

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:38.430
<i>but we were still trying 
to take one small step.</i>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.950
<b>Kuromaru Channel</b>

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.200
Female Idol @ Channel Board

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.210
[Former I-1] Shimada Mayu returns to idol work! [Center]

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.960
I-1's former center Mayushi was in Sendai! 
So surprised!!

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:51.480
Yeah, yeah. Very funny lolol

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.210
Liar lololololololol

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.190
Yeah, yeah. Very funny lolol

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.200
I used to like her

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.220
Mayushi's past her prime

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.220
Mayu lost the center position 
and was exiled to Sendai lololololol

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.220
>>1       No way

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.220
Didn't her family commit suicide?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:02.220
It's true!
She performed in a small concert at Kotodai Park!!

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.720
Pics or it didn't happen

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.710
I can't take pictures of her, 
so I took one of a flier

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.710
I can't take pictures of her, 
so I took one of a flier

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.210
<b>Nanase Yoshino 
Hisami Nanami 
Okamoto Miyu 
Katayama Minami 
Hayashida Airi 
Kikuma Kaya 
Shimada Mayu</b>

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.710
<b>Shimada Mayu</b>

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:26.730
<i>I wanted to find what 
I had once lost here.</i>

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.990
The new year's just begun, 
and I'm already having nightmares?!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.470
I wonder if this

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:23.600
ever falls on anyone's head 
from being pulled too much.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.430
What?

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.280
No way.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.530
I dreamed the shrine's bell

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.860
fell on my head on
 my first visit of the year.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.940
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.190
Good Luck

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.190
Good luck.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:38.940
What'd you get, Mayu?

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.490
Good luck, too.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.200
But my wish...

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.200
Will come true.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.200
Mine, too.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.830
It looks like it's about to snow 
even though it's New Year's.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.810
"It's always sunny 
above the clouds."

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.570
Huh? What's that?

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.720
I found it in a collection 
of witticisms.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.740
Even if the sky 
is covered in clouds,

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.470
it's not as though the sun is gone.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.480
It means once the clouds leave, 
the sun will come out.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.600
Huh.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.030
Hey, could you say it again?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:16.680
Huh?

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.480
"It's always sunny 
above the clouds."

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.540
Who are you texting?

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.370
Matsuda-san.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.990
I think it'll really resonate with him right now.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.740
And send.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.240
<b>Hayashida Airi 

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.250
What gloomy weather.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:40.000
I want to keep doing Wake Up, Girls!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.760
Yeah.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.010
Matsuda-san said he'd be in touch, but...

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.510
I wonder what happened.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.040
Kaya.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.090
Yoppi. You came, too?

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.290
N-No.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.290
I had some free time, 
so I thought I'd see a movie.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.050
Huh.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.670
So austere!

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.690
I really like this song.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.810
I was actually kind of curious.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:42.820
I thought so.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.570
<b>Green Leaves Entertainment</b>

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.700
Matsuda-san's not here.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.280
It's New Year's Day.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.580
Maybe he went home.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.530
Where does he live?

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.330
I don't know.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:02.340
Right. We don't know 
anything about him.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.200
President Sakamaki is believed 
to have fled with the company's funds.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.350
Miyagi police are searching the premises 
regarding charges of embezzlement.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:20.260
The proprietor named his eldest son 
his guarantor without notice,

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:23.400
and under the strain of debt, 
the family was forced to commit suicide.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:23.150
<b>Forced Suicide Due to Debt</b>

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.220
My beloved darling is having an emergency. 
I'm leaving Sendai for a while.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.830
Green Leaves Entertainment 

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.340
What am I supposed to do 
about these bills?

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.870
Damn it, boss...

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:47.260
<b>Barley 
and
Hops</b>

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.280
I'll think about it tomorrow.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.630
I don't want to think 
on New Year's Day.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.190
During the concert, I was so 
concerned with what was in front of me,

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.930
I didn't have time 
to think about the future.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:59.310
I thought it might be 
our first and last concert.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.410
Now that it's over, 
I feel like it's a waste.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:07.280
But keeping up with it seems like 
it would be difficult, too...

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.320
Basically, you want 
to keep doing it, don't you?

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:13.200
Didn't you come to talk 
to Matsuda-san today?

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.200
Huh? I didn't...

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:19.610
The truth is I've been 
thinking about it, too.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.150
It was straightforward of Mayu

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.340
to demand to do it 
because she wanted to.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:27.170
Yeah, that...

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.340
She's faced more challenges than us.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.430
Well, yeah.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.430
Huh? Yoppi and Kayatan.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.470
Miyu!

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.950
Happy New Year!

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.680
What are you two doing?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.680
What are you doing 
on New Year's Day?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.010
I came to ask Matsuda-san 
about the future...

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.620
of Wake Up, Girls! of course.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.190
He's not here.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.690
What? Aww...

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.330
Hello?

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:04.320
What?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.830
Doubts?

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:07.550
I don't have any.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.590
I finally made it 
into an idol group.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.520
What? Do you still have doubts?

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.860
I wouldn't call them doubts.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.090
The way things ended...

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:21.680
You mean the president running away?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:25.730
Lamenting the past 
won't do any good.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.260
You're right.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.860
But the agency might shut down!

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.970
I think that depends on our efforts.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:34.360
What?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.870
I believe talent agencies 
are just like stores.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.870
You know I worked 
at a maid café, right?

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.690
I didn't know.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.120
Me, neither.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.490
Anyway, when the store 
isn't doing well,

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:51.890
sometimes all it takes 
to get back on our feet

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.380
is for the employees 
to work super hard.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.390
What does that have to do with this?

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.430
Huh?

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.340
The agency might not have 
any money right now,

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:06.400
but if we work hard, 
we can get it back on its feet!

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:09.620
A maid café isn't the same 
as the entertainment industry,

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.610
and it's not that easy.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:12.820
Besides,

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:16.150
Matsuda-san doesn't even know 
if he wants to keep the agency open.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.040
I think inspiring 
the boss is up to us, too...

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.090
He's not our boss.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.160
What?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.410
Wh-What?

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.420
Matsuda-san!

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.420
Boss!

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.420
What crazy timing.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.600
Thank you very much.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.420
Sorry for bothering 
you on New Year's Day.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.010
It's all right.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.010
We always work on the 
first day of the year.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:40.680
I see.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.180
Make yourself at home.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.140
It's so good.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.190
Really? That's great.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.690
I'm jealous.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:56.190
Really? I wish my family 
ran a bakery instead.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.490
You're asking for too much.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:59.950
You're right.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.560
I really do want to be an idol...

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.480
Do you want to go to the agency?

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:10.430
It's nearby.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:11.340
Let's check it out.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.070
<b>Matsuda-san</b>

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.060
It's from Matsuda-san.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:15.760
What?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.050
Yes.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.840
Is this you, Minami-chan?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.070
I'm over here.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:26.850
It's dark, and Matsuda-san—oh, 
he's our manager—was flustered,

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.160
so it's blurry.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.870
You have a manager?

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:33.280
You're like a celebrity.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.490
Like a celebrity? 
She is a celebrity, Isokawa-san.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.480
When are you going to perform next?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.290
I don't know yet.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:43.620
What was that?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.930
I don't know yet.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:48.870
I see.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.860
I'm sure I'll hear something soon.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.190
We'll all go see you next time.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.820
Yeah, you should come!

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.060
Minami-chan!

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:02.320
Here!

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.110
Hello?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.390
Matsuda-san?

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:09.640
Huh?

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:21.000
Yes, you are yourself 
and not yourself.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:28.060
I have fallen in love with 
both you and not you.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:31.670
<b>Manager 
Incoming Call</b>

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:35.110
A phone call? Who could it be?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.120
Yes, this is Hisami Nanami.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.370
I am currently busy.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:41.170
Who art thou?

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.730
Thou?

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.680
In any case, I need everyone 
to come to the agency!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.430
What?!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.330
Their name's Sudo-san.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.320
They're a famous producer who 
started a lot of projects.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.690
They saw your Christmas concert.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:59.640
They loved Wake Up, Girls! and said

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:02.450
they'd help us manage the group.

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:06.950
After hearing about Sudo-san's 
background, I was shaking.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.740
That's amazing.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.150
I think my fortune was right.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:13.460
This must be a really lucky year 
if we're getting work already.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:17.240
What does helping with management 
mean, practically speaking?

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.610
Maybe it means getting work for us.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.720
So, what should we do?

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.420
Sudo-san will give you the details

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:27.450
when they come 
to the agency this weekend.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:31.330
They want to speak with 
all of you then, too.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.150
About your direction going forward.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.300
I understand.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.610
Matsuda-san, how do you feel?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:38.480
Huh?

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.440
If they're helping with management,

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.380
that means you'll be 
working together, right?

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.450
Are you going to be okay?

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:47.010
Huh? Well, yeah.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:54.000
Until now, I simply 
obeyed President Tange.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.440
President Tange was 
rough and irresponsible

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:00.130
and ended up running 
away with our money.

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.880
For some reason, 
though, she had major

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.430
connections and found work for us.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.350
Compared to her, I...

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:12.790
I don't have connections, 
money, or confidence.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.270
I'm an all-around loser.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.250
Are you bragging?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.640
But I finally have a chance.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:23.250
I can't afford to turn down 
working with Sudo-san.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.800
I believe I have to do it.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:26.820
What do you think?

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:31.280
Will you work on Wake Up, 
Girls! with me again?

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.920
I already intended to.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.190
All right! I'll do it!

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.180
Well, I'll see how it goes.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:42.300
It depends on the work we get.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.520
You're right.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.800
I'm glad we're working 
again, though.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.050
Right, Mayu?

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.550
Yeah.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.610
All that relief made me hungry.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.390
Do you want to get waffles at Bijou?

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.350
Yeah.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.320
See you this weekend.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:58.440
I'll text you the time.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.330
Okay.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.940
Good work today.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.930
I've experienced nothing but bad 
luck since the day I was born,

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.980
but I finally have a chance.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.450
I'll do everything 
I can for tomorrow!

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:17.760
Matsuda-san's so passionate.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:20.210
It's cute.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.460
I hope it's not for nothing.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.710
You're right.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:28.100
People unaccustomed to 
happiness lose their cool

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.970
when confronted with 
great happiness.

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.970
Nanamin, you're so mature.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.900
Anyway, he doesn't 
have a plan, right?

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.840
He can't help it.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:46.770
President Tange's the one who 
decided to form an idol group.

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.250
Matsuda-san said it himself.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.410
He was just doing as he was told.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.770
I can't believe President Tange 
ran off with the money, though.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:15:00.550
I heard she was taken in by a man.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:02.240
Where did you hear that?

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:06.550
Oh. A lot of well-informed 
people come to my work.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.300
What a crazy information network...

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:11.300
Maybe we really do have to 
rely on this Sudo person.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.310
If we don't get along, we can quit.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:15.570
You're going to quit?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.400
Yeah.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.410
But it's good news.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:20.810
We can work again.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.220
I agree.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.230
Are you watching that again?

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.320
Hey, is that...

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.070
Yeah, the Christmas concert.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:40.970
If we ever make it big, 
that'll be one valuable video.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.200
If we make it big.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.460
If we don't, 
you'll wish you could forget.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.090
Don't say that.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.590
I think it'd be a fun 
experience from our youth.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.590
Hey, Mayu.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:55.210
Do you ever look at videos 
from when you worked with I-1?

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:56.600
Yoppi.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:58.410
Sorry.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.100
No.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:03.340
I see.

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.140
Okay, okay.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:12.050
Let's come up with introductions.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:12.990
Introductions?

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:13.610
Good idea.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.970
Will you listen to mine first?

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:17.920
You've already made one!

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:18.490
That was quick!

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:22.730
I have a few ideas, 
but I haven't chosen one yet.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.870
I want to hear your opinions.

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:26.800
Here I go.

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.550
Welcome home, master.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.880
I will hack into your heart.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:35.640
The Miyu Virus is 
spreading like wildfire!

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:40.390
I'm the twin-tailed and incompetent 
angel of Wake Up, Girls!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.890
Okamoto Miyu!

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:43.930
Huh.

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:44.800
That's great.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.580
It's cute.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.830
It's good.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.400
What's hacking?

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.050
Hello, Sendai!

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.160
We're the I-1 Club!

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:02.180
Today, we have good news for you.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.610
The I-1 Club

00:17:03.610 --> 00:17:08.170
National 47 Prefecture Love 
Connection Project begins today.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:13.690
For this project, the I-1 
Club will go to see you.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:19.430
Here in Miyagi Prefecture's Sendai, 
we'll be building a theater.

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.430
We're so excited to see you.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.690
Look forward to it.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:28.690
This has been a message 
from the I-1 Club!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.750
Seriously? I-1's finally 
building a theater in Sendai.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.960
Who's your favorite?

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.350
Shiho of course.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.560
Me, too.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.700
When I see her smile, I just...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:39.450
Yeah.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.230
I wish she were my girlfriend.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:45.620
I'm home.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.960
Welcome back.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:49.960
I see... A job?

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:52.960
Does this mean you're 
going to keep working?

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:54.070
Yeah.

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:57.270
Mayu-chan, you really do enjoy it.

00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:58.220
Huh?

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:04.310
I mean... you seemed so happy 
when you were singing and dancing.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.710
I think it's a good thing.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:15.060
It means you have 
something you enjoy.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:16.740
Yeah.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:18.790
That's great.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:24.460
Have you told your mother?

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:27.000
I see.

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:30.030
It'll take time.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:59.150
<b>SENDAI Student Metal Band Concert</b>

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:54.930
We're the Sendai-based group, 
Wake Up, Girls!

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:59.150
Um... This is our debut concert.

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:03.120
We were allowed to participate 
in today's concert at the last minute.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.820
We still only have 
one song, but, um...

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.290
We'll sing our hearts out.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.150
Please listen to our song.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:41.650
That's Shimada Mayu!

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:52.460
<i>Believing I could not dream</i>

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:58.590
<i>I protected my small, quiet self</i>

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:05.660
<i>Badly hurt, to the harsh sea</i>

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:10.980
<i>Afraid, I quickly turned my back</i>

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:14.160
<i>But I am who I am</i>

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:17.520
<i>No tricks will work against me</i>

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:23.530
<i>I decided I could only move 
forward without giving up</i>

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:28.950
<i>WAKE UP bathed in bright sunlight</i>

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:36.130
<i>The hope in my heart overlaps with you</i>

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:41.830
<i>STAND UP there is no night 
that does not end</i>

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:48.140
<i>Believe in tomorrow's smile</i>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:54.200
<i>Shine MY ONLY ONE</i>

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:16.790
Cutlet Bowls

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:19.040
I didn't order anything.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:32.610
Su...

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.940
I'm telling you. 
I didn't order any delivery.

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.940
I'm telling you. I didn't...

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.700
Is this Green Leaves?

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.990
S-S-Sudo-san?!

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:11.970
First off... Why don't you try this on?

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

